# ============================================================
#  Numbers (design §8.4). Tier words in effects (`mood +medium`,
#  `rel npc -small`) take their amount from `sizes`; challenge
#  difficulty tiers shift the DC from the expected skill at that
#  point of the run (`curve`, one value per turn, fitted by
#  `node tools/grim.js curve`). All values are tunable.
# ============================================================

@balance
desc: Size tiers are tiny, small, medium, large and huge; skills use the xp row.
sizes: health 3 5 10 16 25 | mood 4 8 13 20 30 | gold 3 8 15 30 60 | renown 2 4 8 13 20 | mana 3 6 10 16 25
  | alignment 3 6 10 16 25 | xp 2 3 6 10 16 | lore 1 1 3 5 8 | rel 1 2 4 6 9 | spark 4 8 13 20 30
difficulty: trivial -15 easy -7 medium 0 hard 8 heroic 16
# Skill XP (design §8.5): the next point costs a + b × level. Fitted so a balanced player averages about 55-60 at the
# end of a four-year run (L: with the spell bonus); a focused skill reaches ~65-75 by month 24 (design ~85: an alarm).
xp_cost: 1 0.04
# Rank XP needed for each promotion (Member → Officer, Officer → Captain), plus performance ≥ 70.
rank_xp: 10 25
weights: health 1 mood 1 gold 0.5 renown 0.8 mana 0.4 alignment 0 xp 1.5 rel 0.6 spark 0.4
# The combat stub (playtest 2, M39, M5): until the minigame, a fight reads arcana, vigor and guile (weighted), plus
# condition × (the mean of health, mood and mana − 50) and spells × total spell levels (at most +15). Entering costs mana.
combat: arcana 1 vigor 1 guile 0.5 condition 0.2 spells 0.75
combat_cost: small
# How far one skill point moves a check's odds (M14): `wild` checks swing whatever your skill; `steady` ones follow it.
swing: normal 2.5 wild 1.2 steady 4
# A shift's pay (M10): `wage` in a job's cards pays the job's `pay:` at your rank × this share.
wage: short 0.5 full 1 overtime 2
# The range a check's odds are clamped to (L-3): a 5% forced fail and a 5% forced success. Milestone checks (a
# `class: milestone` card, an exam) have no forced fail.
odds: min 5 max 95
# Exam preparation (L-3): a course card adds `attend` by itself (options add or cost more); at most `cap` counts.
study: attend 1 cap 15
# A known spell adds `per` to checks of its discipline's skill, at most `cap` (design §9.2; L-3).
spell_check: per 2 cap 6
# Learning a spell, or a level of one, gives skill XP in its discipline (L-6): one tier per spell level.
spell_bonus: medium large huge
# Spark follows friendship (M37): a friendship gain adds spark × (spark / per), at most cap× (partner× for a partner);
# spark crossing `cooldown` asks whether you want it (@game spark_cooldown).
spark_follow: per 25 cap 2 partner 3 cooldown 30
curve: 8 10 11 12 15 15 16 18 19 20 23 23 24 26 27 28 31 31 32 33 34 35 38 38 39 40 41 42 44 45 45 46 47 48 50 51 51 52 53 53 55 55 56 56 57 57 58 59

# ---------------- Presets (design §8.4): named groups of effects ----------------

@preset grind
params: skill
desc: Hard work on one skill.
do:
  $skill +medium
  mood -small
  health -tiny

@preset rest
desc: A real rest.
do:
  mood +medium
  health +small

@preset social
params: who
desc: Time with someone.
do:
  rel $who +small
  mood +small
  gold -tiny

@preset work
desc: Paid work.
do:
  gold +medium
  mood -small
  health -tiny

@preset splurge
desc: Spending to feel better.
do:
  mood +large
  gold -medium

@preset risk
params: res
desc: A gamble: a large gain or a medium loss.
do:
  chance 50:
    $res +large
  else:
    $res -medium
